  "description": "Escape Room is a technical challenge organized by CodeStorm (Fr. CRCE) testing coding, algorithmic problem-solving, debugging, and teamwork under time pressure . Eligibility & Team Guidelines Team Size: 1-2 members . CRCE Students: Both teammates must be from the same class . Non-CRCE Students: Both teammates must be from the same academic year . Cap: Maximum 2 teams allowed per class . Format & Rounds Junior Track (FE / 11th / 12th / Diploma): Vibe Coding Challenge (45 mins): Single round . Build a functional, responsive web solution using HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and permitted AI tools . Participants must bring their own laptops . Evaluation (20 Marks): Functionality (6), Ease of Access (4), Creativity (3), Design (3), Responsiveness (2), Originality (2) . Senior Track (SE / TE / BE): Round 1 – Technical Qualifier (45 mins): SE tackles 2 Debugging + 3 Problem-Solving questions; TE/BE tackles 5 Problem-Solving questions . Round 2 – DSA Escape Challenge (45 mins): Top 25% qualifying teams solve DSA challenges to uncover lock digits and crack the final escape mechanism . Rules & Anti-Cheating Tab-Switching: Monitored automatically during SE/TE/BE rounds . 1st & 2nd Tab Switch: Warnings . 3rd Tab Switch: Direct disqualification . Integrity: Answer sharing, prohibited tools, or interference leads to immediate disqualification . Authority: The organizing committee’s decisions are final .",
